title: "C23 runtime services, platform TLS and cache epochs"
"Static bootstrap capabilities" -> "Native services initialization": "generic TSD and allocator key are separate; keys and lock tables each complete"
"Native services initialization" -> "Runtime Ready(epoch)": "one release after complete prerequisites; initialization callbacks get limited capabilities"
"Runtime Ready(epoch)" -> "Observe same-epoch Ready": "matching acquire/reads-from and metadata lifetime required"
"Observe same-epoch Ready" -> "Known TLS install / cache Ready": "raw Unix void return is not receipt"
"Known TLS install / cache Ready" -> "Fast handle(cache epoch)": "owner scope can cache handle without global per-object pin"
"Fast handle(cache epoch)" -> "Thread close / clear / free": "same-thread fast and platform aliases settled before managed free"
"Thread close / clear / free" -> "Rebind fresh cache epoch": "global services/key stay alive; old request epoch rejected"
"Runtime Ready(epoch)" -> "Public close and cleanup permits": "existing scopes drain; only phase-authorized inherited cleanup continues"
